  "title": "Timbuktu",
  "summary": "Timbuktu, on the edge of the Sahara at the Niger bend in Mali, was founded around 1100 by Tuareg herdsmen and became a major trade city where Saharan salt was exchanged for gold. It was part of the Mali Empire, was taken by Songhai in the 1460s, and was a centre of Islamic learning; Moroccan invaders drove out scholars in the 1500s.",
